  "title": "Away in a Manger",
  "composer": "William J. Kirkpatrick",
  "about": "The words of Away in a Manger are American, and nobody knows who wrote them. Their first two verses were printed in 1882. Many tunes were written for them, and this one is Cradle Song by William J. Kirkpatrick, from 1895. It is the tune sung in Britain, Ireland and Canada.",
  "funFact": "The words were long called Luther's Cradle Hymn, but Martin Luther never wrote them.",
